# repo: signal
# target: .
#
# Make ryohey/signal embeddable: route its MIDI to the embedding page, and turn
# off everything that assumes it is signalmidi.app.
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
# ---------------------
# signal is an application, not a library. There is no npm package, no web
# component and no documented embed API, so the only way to *use* it rather than
# imitate it is to build the app and put the built app in an iframe. That works
# without any patch at all -- but the iframe would then be a self-contained
# sequencer playing its own SoundFont, which is not the point. The point is that
# signal edits the notes and Surge makes the sound.
#
# THE SEAM
# --------
# packages/player defines a two-method `SynthOutput` interface, and
# app/src/services/GroupOutput.ts fans every event out to a list of them. That
# list is how signal already supports sending to a real MIDI port instead of its
# own synth (see app/src/services/MIDIOutput.ts). Everything audible goes through
# it: playback, note previews while drawing, the piano gutter, instrument
# auditions. So this patch adds one more implementation of that interface --
# ParentPortOutput, which posts each event to window.parent -- and selects it.
#
# WHERE THE OUTPUT LIST IS ACTUALLY OWNED (learned the hard way)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# The obvious place to select it is the `synthGroup.outputs.push(...)` in
# RootStore's constructor. That does not work, and fails in a way that looks like
# the bridge is broken rather than bypassed: `updateOutputDevices` in
# stores/reactions.ts REPLACES `synthGroup.outputs` outright, and
# `registerReactions` -- the last statement of the same constructor -- wraps it
# in an `autorun`, which runs immediately. So anything pushed in the constructor
# is discarded microseconds later, and from then on every note goes to the
# SoundFont synth.
#
# What made this confusing to diagnose is that `updateOutputDevices` calls
# `player.allSoundsOff()` BEFORE the reassignment: exactly 16 controller events
# do reach an output pushed by the constructor, and nothing ever does again. A
# bridge that delivers 16 messages and then goes quiet looks like a transport
# fault, and is not.
#
# So the selection lives in `updateOutputDevices`, which is the function that
# owns the list. It is also the better seam: it re-runs when MIDI devices change,
# so the embedder's output survives those changes instead of being dropped.
#
# No editor code is touched. The piano roll, the note model, the WebGL renderer,
# the gestures, the arrange view and the tempo editor are all upstream's.
#
# WHAT "EMBEDDED" MEANS
# --------------------
# `isEmbedded()` in app/src/helpers/platform.ts, alongside upstream's
# `isRunningInElectron()`: true when this document is in a frame. Loaded as a top
# -level page the build behaves exactly as upstream does, SoundFont and all, so
# there is no silent no-sound mode to fall into. Embedded, it additionally:
#
#   - skips SoundFontSynth setup, which is also the only reason the app ever
#     touched a CDN (A320U.sf2 is ~30 MB)
#   - never initialises Firebase, and hides the sign-in button and the sign-up
#     menu item, so no cloud path is reachable
#
# UNCONDITIONAL CHANGES (they apply to this build however it is opened)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - Google Analytics and the Google Fonts stylesheets are removed from
#     edit.html: an embedder must not make third-party requests on someone
#     else's page. Cost: the UI falls back to system fonts.
#   - Sentry is removed from index.tsx, for the same reason.
#   - The service-worker registration is removed, and the generation step with
#     it: it asked for absolute "/service-worker.js" at scope "/edit", which
#     cannot work from a subdirectory.
#   - The build emits relative URLs (base: "./"), minified, without the ~11 MB of
#     source maps, and only the editor entry -- auth.html and community.html are
#     cloud front-ends, and dropping them takes firebaseui out of the bundle.
#     17 MB -> 2.9 MB.
#   - The three dead copies in app/public/ go with them.
#
# NOT upstreamable as-is: removing analytics and Sentry is a fork's decision, not
# a fix. ParentPortOutput and `isEmbedded()` would be.
